    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ag-ui-protocol/ag-ui/zipball/release/2026-09-17",
    "body": "## Packages Published\n### TypeScript (npm) - published at 03:13:24 UTC\n| Package | Version | Install |\n|---------|---------|--------|\n| @ag-ui/claude-agent-sdk | 0.0.4 | `npm install @ag-ui/claude-agent-sdk@0.0.4` |\n| @ag-ui/spring-ai | 0.0.3 | `npm install @ag-ui/spring-ai@0.0.3` |\n| @ag-ui/watsonx | 0.0.2 | `npm install @ag-ui/watsonx@0.0.2` |\n| @ag-ui/a2a-middleware | 0.0.3 | `npm install @ag-ui/a2a-middleware@0.0.3` |\n| create-ag-ui-app | 0.0.59 | `npm install create-ag-ui-app@0.0.59` |\n\n#### @ag-ui/claude-agent-sdk@0.0.4\n\n- Publish the declared MIT license and license file in the npm package.\n\n<!-- ag-ui-published: @ag-ui/claude-agent-sdk@0.0.4 -->\n\n#### @ag-ui/spring-ai@0.0.3\n\n- Publish the declared Apache-2.0 license and license file in the npm package.\n\n<!-- ag-ui-published: @ag-ui/spring-ai@0.0.3 -->\n\n#### @ag-ui/watsonx@0.0.2\n\n- Publish the declared MIT license and license file in the npm package.\n\n<!-- ag-ui-published: @ag-ui/watsonx@0.0.2 -->\n\n#### @ag-ui/a2a-middleware@0.0.3\n\n- Publish the declared MIT license and license file in the npm package.\n\n<!-- ag-ui-published: @ag-ui/a2a-middleware@0.0.3 -->\n\n#### create-ag-ui-app@0.0.59\n\n- Publish the declared MIT license and license file in the npm package.\n\n<!-- ag-ui-published: create-ag-ui-app@0.0.59 -->\n### TypeScript (npm) - published at 18:31:33 UTC\n| Package | Version | Install |\n|---------|---------|--------|\n| @ag-ui/client | 1.0.0 | `npm install @ag-ui/client@1.0.0` |\n| @ag-ui/core | 1.0.0 | `npm install @ag-ui/core@1.0.0` |\n| @ag-ui/encoder | 1.0.0 | `npm install @ag-ui/encoder@1.0.0` |\n| @ag-ui/proto | 1.0.0 | `npm install @ag-ui/proto@1.0.0` |\n\n#### @ag-ui/client@1.0.0\n\n- Adds the 1.0 enforcement pipeline that runs after middleware: strip against the schema and validate.\n- Adds protobuf wire support and compatibility middleware.\n- Snapshot metadata now lets a producer declare only its authoritative activity types, so projectors like A2UI middleware don't delete activity other producers own.\n- MESSAGES_SNAPSHOT now applies in snapshot order instead of appending unseen messages at the end, repairing re-keyed message ordering.\n- Fixes scoped activity deletion without reordering history and preserves full activity snapshot authority.\n- Bounds the replay buffer and caps SSE and protobuf framing buffers to avoid retaining entire responses.\n- Stops upstream reads and cancels the HTTP reader on stream failure, not only on completion.\n- Reasoning events no longer overwrite an activity message sharing the same id.\n- Each run now gets its own set of blocked tool-call IDs, so a stalled run's filtered events are no longer leaked.\n- FilterToolCallsMiddleware clears blocked tool-call IDs on run boundaries.\n- Guards JSON.parse and surfaces stream errors in legacy convert and a2a middleware.\n\n##### Breaking changes\n\n- The wire protocol version is now the generated PROTOCOL_VERSION (\"1.0\").\n- Enforcement pipeline now runs after middleware and strips/validates against the schema, changing which events pass through.\n- MESSAGES_SNAPSHOT ordering and activity-ownership semantics changed; re-verify snapshot handling.\n- Framing buffers are now capped; oversized unbounded streams will error instead of growing.\n\n<!-- ag-ui-published: @ag-ui/client@1.0.0 -->\n\n#### @ag-ui/core@1.0.0\n\n- Rebuilt on generated types; the main entry is now zod-free with validators moved to @ag-ui/core/schemas, making zod an optional peer.\n- 0.x names remain as deprecated aliases of the same types (see DEPRECATIONS.md); content parts are named by what they are rather than by direction.\n- PROTOCOL_VERSION now reads \"1.0\"\n- Ships the AG-UI 1.0 specification, JSON Schema, and the generators SDKs are produced from.\n\n##### Breaking changes\n\n- PROTOCOL_VERSION changed to \"1.0\".\n- Validators moved to @ag-ui/core/schemas; zod is now an optional peer, so imports relying on zod from the main entry must update.\n- Several 0.x type names are now deprecated aliases; re-verify against DEPRECATIONS.md.\n\n<!-- ag-ui-published: @ag-ui/core@1.0.0 -->\n\n#### @ag-ui/encoder@1.0.0\n\n- Updated for the 1.0 release, including generated models, the enforcement pipeline, protobuf wire, and compatibility middleware.\n\n##### Breaking changes\n\nNone.\n\n<!-- ag-ui-published: @ag-ui/encoder@1.0.0 -->\n\n#### @ag-ui/proto@1.0.0\n\n- Updated for the 1.0 release with generated models and protobuf wire support.\n- Protocol version emitted is now \"1.0\", naming the 1.0 schema address.\n\n##### Breaking changes\n\n- Protocol version changed to \"1.0\"; the schema $id address moved to /spec/1.0/schema.json.\n\n<!-- ag-ui-published: @ag-ui/proto@1.0.0 -->\n### Python (PyPI) - published at 18:31:34 UTC\n| Package | Version | Install |\n|---------|---------|--------|\n| ag-ui-protocol | 1.0.0 | `pip install ag-ui-protocol==1.0.0` |\n\n#### ag-ui-protocol@1.0.0\n\n- Froze the draft schema as 1.0; `PROTOCOL_VERSION` now reads \"1.0\", and the schema `$id` moved to `/spec/1.0/schema.json`.\n- `ag_ui.core` re-exports generated 1.0 models, with 0.x names kept as aliases.\n- Added generated models for content parts, tool result parts, capabilities, run outcomes, token usage with cache writes, and file source.\n- Optional null fields are now omitted on serialization; payload nulls are preserved.\n- The single wire protocol version is now the generated `PROTOCOL_VERSION`.\n- Added stable Changelog project URLs to published package metadata on PyPI.\n\n##### Breaking changes\n\n- The wire protocol version changed to \"1.0\"; consumers comparing versions must re-verify.\n- Model names changed to 1.0 names (0.x names remain as aliases); verify imports.\n- The redundant `MetadataMixin` export was removed.\n- Serialization now omits optional nulls, changing emitted payloads.\n\n<!-- ag-ui-published: ag-ui-protocol@1.0.0 -->\n### .NET (NuGet) - published at 18:54:29 UTC\n| Package | Version | Install |\n|---------|---------|--------|\n| AGUI.Abstractions | 1.0.0 | `dotnet add package AGUI.Abstractions --version 1.0.0` |\n| AGUI.Formatting | 1.0.0 | `dotnet add package AGUI.Formatting --version 1.0.0` |\n| AGUI.Protobuf | 1.0.0 | `dotnet add package AGUI.Protobuf --version 1.0.0` |\n| AGUI.Client | 1.0.0 | `dotnet add package AGUI.Client --version 1.0.0` |\n| AGUI.Server | 1.0.0 | `dotnet add package AGUI.Server --version 1.0.0` |\n\n#### AGUI.Abstractions@1.0.0\n\n- Models are now generated from the frozen AG-UI 1.0 JSON Schema, covering content parts, tool result parts, capabilities, run outcomes, token usage with cache writes, and file source.\r\n- `PROTOCOL_VERSION` now reads \"1.0\"; generated headers name the 1.0 schema address.\r\n- Generator emits the `AGUIProtocol` type.\r\n\r\n##### Breaking changes\r\n\r\n- Models renamed to their 1.0 names; verify usages against the generated types.\r\n- Optional nulls are omitted on serialization while payload nulls are preserved.\r\n- Protocol version constant value changed to \"1.0\".\n\n<!-- ag-ui-published: AGUI.Abstractions@1.0.0 -->\n\n#### AGUI.Formatting@1.0.0\n\n- Updated to the generated 1.0 models, aligning content parts, tool result parts, capabilities, run outcomes, and token usage.\r\n\r\n##### Breaking changes\r\n\r\n- Model names and serialization follow the 1.0 schema; re-verify formatting against renamed types and null-omission behavior.\n\n<!-- ag-ui-published: AGUI.Formatting@1.0.0 -->\n\n#### AGUI.Protobuf@1.0.0\n\n- Regenerated against the frozen AG-UI 1.0 schema; protocol version and generated headers now reference the 1.0 address.\r\n\r\n##### Breaking changes\r\n\r\n- Models track the 1.0 schema names; re-verify types and serialization after upgrade.\n\n<!-- ag-ui-published: AGUI.Protobuf@1.0.0 -->\n\n#### AGUI.Client@1.0.0\n\n- Client now declares the protocol version it speaks: every `RunAgentInput` carries \"1.0\", read from the generated `AGUIProtocol.Version`.\r\n- Client validates the producer's protocol version, mirroring the TypeScript client handshake.\r\n- Moved onto the generated 1.0 models.\r\n\r\n##### Breaking changes\r\n\r\n- The protocol version is the generated `AGUI.Abstractions.AGUIProtocol.Version`; there is no hand-written constant beside it.\r\n- Wire protocol version now sent as \"1.0\"; model names and null handling follow the 1.0 schema.\n\n<!-- ag-ui-published: AGUI.Client@1.0.0 -->\n\n#### AGUI.Server@1.0.0\n\n- Moved onto the generated 1.0 models.\r\n- Added typed access to AG-UI client state.\r\n\r\n##### Breaking changes\r\n\r\n- Models track the 1.0 schema names; re-verify types and serialization behavior after upgrade.\n\n<!-- ag-ui-published: AGUI.Server@1.0.0 -->\n\n\n",
